{"parentUuid":"19e9e7b3-81d9-43c4-a57a-5e2a6cb63835","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md","content":{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"@AGENTS.md\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false},"displayPath":"CLAUDE.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0dca7035-d132-4bdd-af65-d0c3a5b84ffe","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:37:45.713Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md:\n\n@AGENTS.md\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"0dca7035-d132-4bdd-af65-d0c3a5b84ffe","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/AGENTS.md","content":{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: Flint\n\n## What this is\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\npartner. This repo builds the knowledge base behind that role. It catalogs Eric's\nDrive (his own material, TB's Training Info, Landon Evans, courses, papers), routes the\nhigh-value sources into Zotero and the SecondBrain vault, and writes per-discipline\nsynthesis notes that compare the sources against Eric's own method. It is a side-lane\nproject, outside the prioritization-slate cap. See `README.md` for the approach and\n`docs/PLAN.md` for the checklist.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- `data/` is gitignored except aggregate summaries. Regenerate the file-level manifest with `pwsh scripts/build_manifest.ps1`.\n- Codex workers read staged copies in `staging/`, never the Drive root. DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports are never catalogued.\n- The ingest review gate has two stages.\n  1. Before atomizing, verify the source artifact by an independent route: page order, scanned versus text, transcripts checked against captions.\n  2. Before promoting, Codex reviews the staged entries against the staged sources, with instructions to falsify (`staging/review_<source>_codex.md`). Nothing reaches the vault without a GO or a GO AFTER FIXES that has been applied.\n- Library entries label every voice. The source author's statements are plain. Eric's judgments get \"Eric's review:\". The entry writer's own reasoning gets \"Inference:\". No unlabeled judgments. Every number carries a timestamp or page the reviewer can check, and a claim is only tagged \"confirmed in PDF\" if that PDF is staged. (Learned from the Harries review, 2026-09-26: 25 of 35 files needed fixes, mostly for attribution.)\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false,"parent":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md"},"displayPath":"AGENTS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6f15a8d6-3bda-49c0-85b9-b1704abb2574","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:37:45.713Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/AGENTS.md:\n\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: Flint\n\n## What this is\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\npartner. This repo builds the knowledge base behind that role. It catalogs Eric's\nDrive (his own material, TB's Training Info, Landon Evans, courses, papers), routes the\nhigh-value sources into Zotero and the SecondBrain vault, and writes per-discipline\nsynthesis notes that compare the sources against Eric's own method. It is a side-lane\nproject, outside the prioritization-slate cap. See `README.md` for the approach and\n`docs/PLAN.md` for the checklist.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- `data/` is gitignored except aggregate summaries. Regenerate the file-level manifest with `pwsh scripts/build_manifest.ps1`.\n- Codex workers read staged copies in `staging/`, never the Drive root. DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports are never catalogued.\n- The ingest review gate has two stages.\n  1. Before atomizing, verify the source artifact by an independent route: page order, scanned versus text, transcripts checked against captions.\n  2. Before promoting, Codex reviews the staged entries against the staged sources, with instructions to falsify (`staging/review_<source>_codex.md`). Nothing reaches the vault without a GO or a GO AFTER FIXES that has been applied.\n- Library entries label every voice. The source author's statements are plain. Eric's judgments get \"Eric's review:\". The entry writer's own reasoning gets \"Inference:\". No unlabeled judgments. Every number carries a timestamp or page the reviewer can check, and a claim is only tagged \"confirmed in PDF\" if that PDF is staged. (Learned from the Harries review, 2026-09-26: 25 of 35 files needed fixes, mostly for attribution.)\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
