{"parentUuid":"da7e0a83-64fc-4176-b2fd-89aadfa5b3a0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a9f69a56-41de-4fd2-88ce-bc0e210b67cb","agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016ZUf4QZFMLJGkQcCD2VQg4","type":"tool_result","content":"5:that unidirectional training over periods as long as 4-12 weeks can be very effective, especially if the intensity is \n13:training. In this context, the loading may be considered concentrated if its volume in the month in which it is \n14:applied constitutes 23-25% of the general volume for the year.\n20:supercompensate to the desired level o f preparedness. The gains elicited, for instance, by 4-8 week concentrated \n22:weeks, so it is essential for the athlete not to lose patience and hasten into the next concentrated phase without \n---381\n22:weeks) of training can be very effective. Use of a variety of means, especially when applied with a gradual \n30:unidirectional loading for a limited period (of up to 2 months). This concentrated influence produces a brief, \n36:means already intensifies the training. The loading may be defined as concentrated if its volume in the month in \n37:which it is concentrated is 23-25% of the general annual volume.\n---375\n11:the LDTE was observed to last from 4-12 weeks during the long-term stages of strength preparation.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5eb50a2d-e73b-487a-9a82-90422cdd6dd2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:40:38.592Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"5:that unidirectional training over periods as long as 4-12 weeks can be very effective, especially if the intensity is \n13:training. In this context, the loading may be considered concentrated if its volume in the month in which it is \n14:applied constitutes 23-25% of the general volume for the year.\n20:supercompensate to the desired level o f preparedness. The gains elicited, for instance, by 4-8 week concentrated \n22:weeks, so it is essential for the athlete not to lose patience and hasten into the next concentrated phase without \n---381\n22:weeks) of training can be very effective. Use of a variety of means, especially when applied with a gradual \n30:unidirectional loading for a limited period (of up to 2 months). This concentrated influence produces a brief, \n36:means already intensifies the training. The loading may be defined as concentrated if its volume in the month in \n37:which it is concentrated is 23-25% of the general annual volume.\n---375\n11:the LDTE was observed to last from 4-12 weeks during the long-term stages of strength preparation.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"da7e0a83-64fc-4176-b2fd-89aadfa5b3a0","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
