]]*\\]\\]\" $f","description":"Replace \"entry above\" with wikilink"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffo6q6j2HEHj8Q3oj6o6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1ffeffcf-0f34-42bb-8b88-77d8493022c9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:42:37.797Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"1ffeffcf-0f34-42bb-8b88-77d8493022c9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"a9f69a56-41de-4fd2-88ce-bc0e210b67cb","agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EpyyLUMW8tfLxj3EoazQkq","type":"tool_result","content":"27:as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"40f72d7b-bf6a-40e2-a2af-292df1079a7f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:42:38.069Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"27:as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":24,"oldLines":7,"newStart":24,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **When to apply** — Inference: plan the stage after any deliberately heavy block as a change of content, not only a cut in load: lower volume of special means, more general work. Inference: size its length to the block before it, longer after a longer or heavier block. Eric's baseline: \"Recovery capacity must be 'earned' by training hard enough first\" (`docs/method-baseline.md` line 151, Inferred (transcript)). Inference: the authors' rule is the other half of that statement: once the hard block has been done, the restorative stage is part of the plan."," ","-**When NOT to apply** — No durations are given for the restorative stage here. In 5.3.3 the book gives a 1-3 week latency to gains after 4-8 week concentrated blocks (PDF p. 305 / printed p. 294; see [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]), and on the page before this one a 7-10 day pause between blocks and a longer, unspecified recuperation after three blocks (PDF p. 360 / printed p. 349). Bompa & Haff state a similar scaling rule (\"the greater the magnitude and duration of the concentrated loading phase, the more time needed for fatigue to dissipate and performance to improve\"), as quoted in the 5.3.3 entry above; that is agreement on direction, not on a number. Inference: \"GPP\" here is not defined; the means chosen should still not undo the quality just built.","+**When NOT to apply** — No durations are given for the restorative stage here. In 5.3.3 the book gives a 1-3 week latency to gains after 4-8 week concentrated blocks (PDF p. 305 / printed p. 294; see [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]), and on the page before this one a 7-10 day pause between blocks and a longer, unspecified recuperation after three blocks (PDF p. 360 / printed p. 349). Bompa & Haff state a similar scaling rule (\"the greater the magnitude and duration of the concentrated loading phase, the more time needed for fatigue to dissipate and performance to improve\"), as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]; that is agreement on direction, not on a number. Inference: \"GPP\" here is not defined; the means chosen should still not undo the quality just built."," "," **Example** — The authors give no worked case. Inference: after a three-week concentrated jump and strength block, a sprinter's next week drops the depth jumps and heavy squats, keeps short sprints, and adds general circuits and aerobic work."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1ffeffcf-0f34-42bb-8b88-77d8493022c9","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
