{"parentUuid":"921f0360-a3db-4590-ae59-28e082cfdbc3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffotFMVvDC7BozhZbCdY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016FmZAvaJsJ9nMYrArfX9sB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md","content":"# Fixes applied: Supertraining 6.4-6.8.2 (Ch6b), 16 entries\n\nFixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03. Review: `staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md` (round 1, GO AFTER FIXES: 11 FIX rows, 7 numbered fix groups, 4 reciprocal-link suggestions, 5 missing ideas).\nSource checked: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`. I extracted the text of PDF idx 305, 327, 347-362, 370, 371, 375 and 381 with PyMuPDF (`staging/_tmp/f6b_text.txt`). I rendered and opened PDF 305, 348, 351, 358, 359, 360, 361, 362, 375 and 381 (`staging/_renders/f6b_p<N>.png`), plus a 400 dpi crop of Fig 6.22 (`staging/_renders/f6b_p358_fig622_400.png`). Page key: PDF idx = printed + 11.\nScope: the 16 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`. I edited the 11 flagged entries plus two GO entries (`principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window`, for the PDF 359 locator, the Bompa wording and a review-suggested reciprocal link; `heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance`, for a dangling \"entry above\" pointer). No new entries, so the scope file is unchanged (16 lines). No renames. I did not edit `_book.md`, any 6a, 6c or 6d file, or the vault.\n\n## Fig 6.22 reading (decided from the image)\n\nGraph A (thick line, \"Fitness state\") on the 400 dpi crop of PDF 358 / p.347: it starts at about y = 660 px (Year 1 left edge), is at about 440 px at the Year 1/2 boundary, about 285 px at the Year 2/3 boundary and about 200 px at the right edge. The rise is about 225 px in Year 1, about 155 px in Year 2 and about 80 px in Year 3. At the Year 1/2 boundary A sits about 70 px above the straight chord from start to end. So A is a decelerating (concave) curve, consistent with the text's \"parabola whose peak is eventually reached with time\" (PDF 359). No peak is drawn within the three years. The review is right and the writer's \"nearly straight\" reading was wrong; both Fig 6.22 fixes were applied.\n\n| file | what changed |\n|---|---|\n| framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md | **Fix 6 + 5.** The \"(shaded box A)\" and \"(shaded box B)\" parentheticals are removed from the Fig 6.12 walk-through. A new sentence describes \"the shaded band A (Training Load, Training Potential of Loading, Athlete's Fitness State) and the shaded region B (Athlete's Fitness State, Training Effect of Loading, Athlete's External Interactions), which overlap at fitness state\" (checked against the PDF 348 image). Why it works now opens: \"The authors set out a one-way chain (load, fitness state, external interactions) and control at two levels (PDF p. 348 / printed p. 337). Inference: fitness state is therefore the only route from load to result, so both links need measuring.\" |\n| heuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md | **Fix 6.** Fig 6.15 now reads: \"one broad inverted-U ...; a narrow spike A at low arousal; a second hump B on the right-hand slope of the broad curve ('second wind'); and a narrow spike C at high arousal\" (checked against the PDF 351 image). Point 2 adds: \"The book gives no source for the personality difference; it is presented as a general claim ('appears'), not as the authors' finding.\" The optional Eysenck and 1908 provenance notes were not added (they need a checked citation). |\n| framework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming.md | **Fix 6.** When NOT now says the authors call for subdivision (\"One should further subdivide the sports in each of these broad groups\") only within the acyclic and cyclic groups, before they introduce the third group (PDF 357 / p.346), and that \"extending it to the complex group is this entry's inference\". Verified in the text layer: the call sits between the cyclic bullet and \"Finally, one should identify a third group\". |\n| principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md | **Fix 5 + 4.** Why it works now reads: \"The authors' stated basis is 'modern sporting requirements' and 'common sense' (PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347); they give no study. Inference: the effects they go on to describe ... unfold over weeks, so microcycle-to-microcycle comparison would misread them.\" The batch 6a sentence is deleted. In its place: the book calls the training session \"the fundamental unit\" in 6.2 (PDF 327 / p.316, confirmed in the text layer) and the mesocycle the fundamental unit in 6.8.1 (PDF 358); \"the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit. Inference: the book does not reconcile the wording\". Link to [[framework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap]] added there and in Related (review's reciprocal-link suggestion). |\n| claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md | **Fix 1 + 7, missing idea 5.** \"a thick, nearly straight rising line A\" is now \"a thick rising line A ... whose slope shrinks each year (steepest in Year 1, flattest in Year 3)\". \"a high-resolution crop\" is now \"a 400 dpi crop\". The \"Figure against text\" sentence is replaced with \"Graph A flattens year by year, in line with the text's 'parabola whose peak is eventually reached with time' (PDF p. 359 / printed p. 348); no peak is drawn within the three years.\" All three \"text layer only\" locators for PDF 359 now read \"checked against the page image\" (I opened the page). Missing idea 5 is folded into the endurance caveat: the problem lies \"in the ability to observe it in the factors used for analysis\", with the full \"measures of aerobic and anaerobic output ... do not express the internal changes associated with adaptation to intense cyclic or acyclic work\" quote, plus a labelled Inference on what that means for conditioning tests. |\n| claim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md | **Fix 1 + 6 + 7.** The PDF 359 locator now reads \"checked against the page image\". Why it works now says research on adaptation (Folbrot, Selye) \"has to be taken much further in its application to the development of sporting mastery, especially in endurance sports\"; until then they assume \"the same, above-mentioned chief mechanisms ...\". When NOT: the \"Page 359 was read from the text layer only\" sentence and the \"graph A looks nearly straight\" clause are deleted, replaced with \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year, consistent with the parabola, but no peak is drawn within the three years (PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347).\" |\n| principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md | **GO row, minor items applied.** PDF 359 locator now \"checked against the page image\". The Bompa comparison now reads \"sets out three outcomes of loading (an increasing, varied load, adaptation; an unchanging load, plateau; an excessive one, maladaptation)\", checked against the vault `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold` (\"a *standard* (unchanging) load ⇒ plateau\"). Related adds the review's reciprocal link [[principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue]]. |\n| framework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md | **Fix 2.** (1) The dip-versus-block sentence is replaced: Panel B's depression lasts until about weeks 7-9 of 18, which fits \"concentrated in the first half of the training phase\" (PDF 360); the figure marks 6-week intervals (dashed lines at weeks 6 and 12) and shows no 3-4 week blocks or 7-10 day pauses, so it does not illustrate the block durations; its x-axis ends at 18 weeks against the text's 18-22 (all checked on the PDF 360 and 361 images). (2) \"Issurin (2016) judged the evidence for Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model insufficient ...\" (the vault Issurin brief, line 51, says the CU model is Verkhoshansky's). (3) \"Not for novices or medium-level athletes, by the authors' own scope\" is replaced with: devised for highly qualified athletes (PDF 360); in 6.9.5 \"both methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification\" (PDF p. 371 / printed p. 360, text layer), \"so it is not required there\". I also changed the When to apply Inference, which said \"distributed loading for medium-level athletes\", to \"distributed loading when performance must hold; at medium qualification the authors say both forms work\". Reciprocal link [[claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes]] added in When NOT and Related. `contested` stays, for the Issurin reason. |\n| heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md | **Fix 3.** The When NOT conflict paragraph is rewritten by quantity. **Concentrated block length (the conflict):** 3-4 weeks (PDF 360, given as the \"determined\" optimum), \"for instance, ... 4-8 week concentrated blocks\" (PDF 305, image checked) and \"a limited period (of up to 2 months)\" (PDF 381, image checked). **Different quantities:** 4-12 week unidirectional *stage* (PDF 305, 381); 4-12 week LDTE duration, \"approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\" (PDF 375 / p.364, image checked); 1-3 week latency (PDF 305); 18-22 week stage to exhaust the CAR (PDF 360); per-quality upper limits in [[claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality]]. The 9-12 week reconciliation is kept as Inference, now framed as linking block length to stage length. New Inference: both 5.3.3 and 6.12.2 define concentration by one month's volume (23-25%, PDF 305 and 381, quoted), so the month is the working unit and \"up to 2 months\" reads as a ceiling. The PDF 381 \"text layer only\" locator is gone. The \"Unclear arithmetic\" note is unchanged. Related adds the time-limits link. `contested` kept (see Disagreements 1). |\n| heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md | **GO row, minor item applied.** \"as quoted in the 5.3.3 entry above\" is now \"as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]\". |\n| claim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md | **Fix 4 + 5.** The batch 6a sentence is replaced with \"The 6.2.2 intensity-zone material and Table 6.1 it points to are at PDF pp. 334-335 / printed pp. 323-324 (6.2.2 opens on PDF p. 334; Table 6.1 is on PDF p. 335)\" (checked in the text layer; see Disagreements 3). Why it works now opens \"Inference: Bondarchuk's study as reported does not test intensity at all ...\". |\n| principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md | **Fix 5 + 6.** The Zhurbinoi passage is now quoted in full, both sentences, with \"(Zhurbinoi, 1978)\" where the source puts it (closing the second sentence; PDF 362 image). Why it works now reads: \"For the cyclic side the authors cite Zhurbinoi (1978) on strength-endurance (PDF p. 362 / printed p. 351); the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only. Inference: Chapter 4's argument ... supports the same point.\" |\n| claim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov.md | **Fix 6.** Title is now \"Training Emphasis Shifts With Qualification: Sprinters Move From Aerobic Endurance and Speed to Speed Endurance; for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic (Vankov 1978)\". In When NOT, \"The distance-runner sentence\" is now \"The distance-athlete sentence ('distance athletes', not runners)\". Slug unchanged (it says \"distance\", not \"runners\"), so no rename. |\n\n## Missing ideas: placement\n\n| # | idea | placement |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Decision-making and problem-solving (PDF 355-356) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The H/M/L rating, six steps, Maier and Roskin are framed for \"managers or committees\"; the page has no coach, athlete or training example. |\n| 2 | Management versus leadership; Oncken's authority types (PDF 350, 353) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The only sport mention is an illustration of the terms (team captains lead on the field, managers off it); nothing applies it to training. |\n| 3 | Blake-Mouton grid, Tannenbaum-Schmidt continuum, Likert (PDF 353-355) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The grid coordinates are given for generic management styles. The nearby \"applied by managers, leaders and coaches steeped in the traditional ways\" refers to the Fig 6.17 traditional model, as a criticism, not to the grid, and gives no training use. |\n| 4 | Needs theories (PDF 352) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The one athlete note (world-class performances in altered states, Murphy & White 1978) describes transcendence; it is not applied to training. The \"applied with circumspection\" warning concerns Maslow's model in general. |\n| 5 | Endurance monitoring limit (PDF 359) | **Folded into** `claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation` (its When NOT already held the endurance caveat from the same paragraph), with a labelled Inference. |\n\nNo new entry was written, so `_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt` is unchanged.\n\n## Reciprocal links (within 6b files only; all targets exist in the book folder)\n\n- distributed-vs-concentrated → [[claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes]]: added.\n- concentrated-blocks → [[claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality]]: added. [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]] was already in Related; it is now also cited in the conflict paragraph for the PDF 375 duration.\n- mesocycle → [[framework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap]]: added.\n- adaptation-reserve-window → [[principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue]]: added.\n- The back-links from those 6c/6d/6a files to the 6b entries are for their own fixers or the coordinator; I did not edit them.\n\n## Disagreements with the review\n\n1. **Block lengths: `contested` kept, but the conflict is narrower than the review states.** The review calls 3-4 weeks, 4-8 weeks and \"up to 2 months\" one quantity in conflict. On the pages, 4-8 weeks (PDF 305, offered \"for instance\") and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381, a ceiling) agree with each other. The real conflict is 3-4 weeks, which PDF 360 presents as the determined optimum, against blocks up to twice that long in 5.3.3. The entry now says so explicitly. It still counts as a conflict on one quantity, so `contested` stays.\n2. **PDF 375 adds a link the review did not mention.** PDF 375 says the LDTE duration \"is approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\". So the 4-12 week LDTE figure and the 4-12 week stage figure are tied by the book itself; they are still different quantities from block length. Quoted in the entry.\n3. **Bondarchuk page range.** The review's correction text gives \"PDF pp. 334-336 / printed pp. 323-325\". The text layer puts the 6.2.2 heading on PDF 334 and Table 6.1 (its reference and caption) on PDF 335; nothing for either is on 336. The entry says pp. 334-335 / printed 323-324.\n4. **Fig 6.22:** no disagreement. My own measurement agrees with the review (see the reading above).\n5. **Optional items not applied.** Expectancy (Tellier provenance note) and situational leadership (\"Inference:\" prefix) are GO rows with optional suggestions, and arousal's Eysenck/1908 notes need a checked citation. None was applied. I did apply two minor GO-row items: the adaptation-reserve entry (the PDF 359 locator the review asked for, and the Bompa wording, verified against the vault file) and the restorative-stage pointer (a dangling \"above\" in a standalone note).\n\nEvery other review claim held up on the page: Fig 6.12 shaded regions (PDF 348), Fig 6.15 hump B (PDF 351), \"further subdivide\" placement (PDF 357), the \"fundamental unit\" pair (PDF 327, 358), the PDF 359 text matching the image, \"taken much further\" about research (PDF 359), Fig 6.23 dashed lines and no drawn blocks (PDF 361), the PDF 371 medium-qualification sentence, the Zhurbinoi placement and the absence of a Chapter 4 pointer (PDF 362), and \"distance athletes\" (PDF 362).\n\n## Checks\n\nGrep proof, run from the book folder (new wording, one line per change):\n\n```\nframework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md:23:which overlap at fitness state\nframework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md:31:Inference: fitness state is therefore the only route\nheuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md:23:a second hump B on the right-hand slope\nheuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md:18:The book gives no source for the personality difference\nframework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming.md:27:extending it to the complex group is this entry's inference\nprinciple--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md:25:The authors' stated basis is \"modern sporting requirements\"\nprinciple--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md:29:the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:22:whose slope shrinks each year\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:28:Graph A flattens year by year\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:28:they do not express the internal changes\nclaim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md:25:research on adaptation (Folbrot, Selye)\nclaim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md:29:Graph A's slope shrinks each year, consistent with the parabola\nprinciple--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md:22:an unchanging load, plateau\nprinciple--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md:30:loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:Panel B's depression lasts until about weeks 7-9 of 18\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:so it is not required there\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:Contested inside the book (concentrated block length)\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:Different quantities, not part of the conflict\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:which makes the month the working unit\nheuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md:27:as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration\nclaim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md:24:6.2.2 opens on PDF p. 334\nclaim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md:20:Inference: Bondarchuk's study as reported\nprinciple--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md:22:the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\nprinciple--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md:20:accelerate the increase in functional strength (Zhurbinoi, 1978)\nclaim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov.md:14:for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic\n```\n\nOld phrases, count of 6b files still holding each (all 0):\n\n```\nshaded box A: 0\nspikes B and C: 0\nown call to \"further subdivide\" applies: 0\nBatch 6a: 0\nbatch 6a: 0\nnearly straight: 0\ntext layer only: 0\nNot for novices or medium-level: 0\nFigure against text: the figure: 0\nDistance Runners Add: 0\npoint to Chapter 4: 0\n5.3.3 entry above: 0\nhas to be taken much further,\" assuming: 0\n```\n\n`grep -i batch` over the 16 6b files: no matches.\n\nMechanical greps over the 16 scoped files (run under `/bin/bash`):\n\n```\n== em dashes not in section headers:\n(end)\n== header em-dash count per file:\n  16 6\n== wrapped wikilinks:\n(end)\n== CR endings:\n0\n```\n\nAll wikilink targets resolve (the four `old-bull-performance-course--old-bull/...` targets are in the vault under `performance-technology-and-leadership/`).\n\nLint, run from the Flint root:\n\n```\n$ ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\n\nNo 6b file appears in the lint output. The one issue is the known `_book.md` false positive (title and table dashes), outside scope and not edited.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3665,"cache_read_input_tokens":179890,"output_tokens":8388,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":32},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3665},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8388,"cache_read_input_tokens":179890,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3665,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016FmZAvaJsJ9nMYrArfX9sB":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md","content":"# Fixes applied: Supertraining 6.4-6.8.2 (Ch6b), 16 entries\n\nFixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03. Review: `staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md` (round 1, GO AFTER FIXES: 11 FIX rows, 7 numbered fix groups, 4 reciprocal-link suggestions, 5 missing ideas).\nSource checked: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`. I extracted the text of PDF idx 305, 327, 347-362, 370, 371, 375 and 381 with PyMuPDF (`staging/_tmp/f6b_text.txt`). I rendered and opened PDF 305, 348, 351, 358, 359, 360, 361, 362, 375 and 381 (`staging/_renders/f6b_p<N>.png`), plus a 400 dpi crop of Fig 6.22 (`staging/_renders/f6b_p358_fig622_400.png`). Page key: PDF idx = printed + 11.\nScope: the 16 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`. I edited the 11 flagged entries plus two GO entries (`principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window`, for the PDF 359 locator, the Bompa wording and a review-suggested reciprocal link; `heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance`, for a dangling \"entry above\" pointer). No new entries, so the scope file is unchanged (16 lines). No renames. I did not edit `_book.md`, any 6a, 6c or 6d file, or the vault.\n\n## Fig 6.22 reading (decided from the image)\n\nGraph A (thick line, \"Fitness state\") on the 400 dpi crop of PDF 358 / p.347: it starts at about y = 660 px (Year 1 left edge), is at about 440 px at the Year 1/2 boundary, about 285 px at the Year 2/3 boundary and about 200 px at the right edge. The rise is about 225 px in Year 1, about 155 px in Year 2 and about 80 px in Year 3. At the Year 1/2 boundary A sits about 70 px above the straight chord from start to end. So A is a decelerating (concave) curve, consistent with the text's \"parabola whose peak is eventually reached with time\" (PDF 359). No peak is drawn within the three years. The review is right and the writer's \"nearly straight\" reading was wrong; both Fig 6.22 fixes were applied.\n\n| file | what changed |\n|---|---|\n| framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md | **Fix 6 + 5.** The \"(shaded box A)\" and \"(shaded box B)\" parentheticals are removed from the Fig 6.12 walk-through. A new sentence describes \"the shaded band A (Training Load, Training Potential of Loading, Athlete's Fitness State) and the shaded region B (Athlete's Fitness State, Training Effect of Loading, Athlete's External Interactions), which overlap at fitness state\" (checked against the PDF 348 image). Why it works now opens: \"The authors set out a one-way chain (load, fitness state, external interactions) and control at two levels (PDF p. 348 / printed p. 337). Inference: fitness state is therefore the only route from load to result, so both links need measuring.\" |\n| heuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md | **Fix 6.** Fig 6.15 now reads: \"one broad inverted-U ...; a narrow spike A at low arousal; a second hump B on the right-hand slope of the broad curve ('second wind'); and a narrow spike C at high arousal\" (checked against the PDF 351 image). Point 2 adds: \"The book gives no source for the personality difference; it is presented as a general claim ('appears'), not as the authors' finding.\" The optional Eysenck and 1908 provenance notes were not added (they need a checked citation). |\n| framework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming.md | **Fix 6.** When NOT now says the authors call for subdivision (\"One should further subdivide the sports in each of these broad groups\") only within the acyclic and cyclic groups, before they introduce the third group (PDF 357 / p.346), and that \"extending it to the complex group is this entry's inference\". Verified in the text layer: the call sits between the cyclic bullet and \"Finally, one should identify a third group\". |\n| principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md | **Fix 5 + 4.** Why it works now reads: \"The authors' stated basis is 'modern sporting requirements' and 'common sense' (PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347); they give no study. Inference: the effects they go on to describe ... unfold over weeks, so microcycle-to-microcycle comparison would misread them.\" The batch 6a sentence is deleted. In its place: the book calls the training session \"the fundamental unit\" in 6.2 (PDF 327 / p.316, confirmed in the text layer) and the mesocycle the fundamental unit in 6.8.1 (PDF 358); \"the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit. Inference: the book does not reconcile the wording\". Link to [[framework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap]] added there and in Related (review's reciprocal-link suggestion). |\n| claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md | **Fix 1 + 7, missing idea 5.** \"a thick, nearly straight rising line A\" is now \"a thick rising line A ... whose slope shrinks each year (steepest in Year 1, flattest in Year 3)\". \"a high-resolution crop\" is now \"a 400 dpi crop\". The \"Figure against text\" sentence is replaced with \"Graph A flattens year by year, in line with the text's 'parabola whose peak is eventually reached with time' (PDF p. 359 / printed p. 348); no peak is drawn within the three years.\" All three \"text layer only\" locators for PDF 359 now read \"checked against the page image\" (I opened the page). Missing idea 5 is folded into the endurance caveat: the problem lies \"in the ability to observe it in the factors used for analysis\", with the full \"measures of aerobic and anaerobic output ... do not express the internal changes associated with adaptation to intense cyclic or acyclic work\" quote, plus a labelled Inference on what that means for conditioning tests. |\n| claim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md | **Fix 1 + 6 + 7.** The PDF 359 locator now reads \"checked against the page image\". Why it works now says research on adaptation (Folbrot, Selye) \"has to be taken much further in its application to the development of sporting mastery, especially in endurance sports\"; until then they assume \"the same, above-mentioned chief mechanisms ...\". When NOT: the \"Page 359 was read from the text layer only\" sentence and the \"graph A looks nearly straight\" clause are deleted, replaced with \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year, consistent with the parabola, but no peak is drawn within the three years (PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347).\" |\n| principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md | **GO row, minor items applied.** PDF 359 locator now \"checked against the page image\". The Bompa comparison now reads \"sets out three outcomes of loading (an increasing, varied load, adaptation; an unchanging load, plateau; an excessive one, maladaptation)\", checked against the vault `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold` (\"a *standard* (unchanging) load ⇒ plateau\"). Related adds the review's reciprocal link [[principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue]]. |\n| framework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md | **Fix 2.** (1) The dip-versus-block sentence is replaced: Panel B's depression lasts until about weeks 7-9 of 18, which fits \"concentrated in the first half of the training phase\" (PDF 360); the figure marks 6-week intervals (dashed lines at weeks 6 and 12) and shows no 3-4 week blocks or 7-10 day pauses, so it does not illustrate the block durations; its x-axis ends at 18 weeks against the text's 18-22 (all checked on the PDF 360 and 361 images). (2) \"Issurin (2016) judged the evidence for Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model insufficient ...\" (the vault Issurin brief, line 51, says the CU model is Verkhoshansky's). (3) \"Not for novices or medium-level athletes, by the authors' own scope\" is replaced with: devised for highly qualified athletes (PDF 360); in 6.9.5 \"both methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification\" (PDF p. 371 / printed p. 360, text layer), \"so it is not required there\". I also changed the When to apply Inference, which said \"distributed loading for medium-level athletes\", to \"distributed loading when performance must hold; at medium qualification the authors say both forms work\". Reciprocal link [[claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes]] added in When NOT and Related. `contested` stays, for the Issurin reason. |\n| heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md | **Fix 3.** The When NOT conflict paragraph is rewritten by quantity. **Concentrated block length (the conflict):** 3-4 weeks (PDF 360, given as the \"determined\" optimum), \"for instance, ... 4-8 week concentrated blocks\" (PDF 305, image checked) and \"a limited period (of up to 2 months)\" (PDF 381, image checked). **Different quantities:** 4-12 week unidirectional *stage* (PDF 305, 381); 4-12 week LDTE duration, \"approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\" (PDF 375 / p.364, image checked); 1-3 week latency (PDF 305); 18-22 week stage to exhaust the CAR (PDF 360); per-quality upper limits in [[claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality]]. The 9-12 week reconciliation is kept as Inference, now framed as linking block length to stage length. New Inference: both 5.3.3 and 6.12.2 define concentration by one month's volume (23-25%, PDF 305 and 381, quoted), so the month is the working unit and \"up to 2 months\" reads as a ceiling. The PDF 381 \"text layer only\" locator is gone. The \"Unclear arithmetic\" note is unchanged. Related adds the time-limits link. `contested` kept (see Disagreements 1). |\n| heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md | **GO row, minor item applied.** \"as quoted in the 5.3.3 entry above\" is now \"as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]\". |\n| claim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md | **Fix 4 + 5.** The batch 6a sentence is replaced with \"The 6.2.2 intensity-zone material and Table 6.1 it points to are at PDF pp. 334-335 / printed pp. 323-324 (6.2.2 opens on PDF p. 334; Table 6.1 is on PDF p. 335)\" (checked in the text layer; see Disagreements 3). Why it works now opens \"Inference: Bondarchuk's study as reported does not test intensity at all ...\". |\n| principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md | **Fix 5 + 6.** The Zhurbinoi passage is now quoted in full, both sentences, with \"(Zhurbinoi, 1978)\" where the source puts it (closing the second sentence; PDF 362 image). Why it works now reads: \"For the cyclic side the authors cite Zhurbinoi (1978) on strength-endurance (PDF p. 362 / printed p. 351); the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only. Inference: Chapter 4's argument ... supports the same point.\" |\n| claim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov.md | **Fix 6.** Title is now \"Training Emphasis Shifts With Qualification: Sprinters Move From Aerobic Endurance and Speed to Speed Endurance; for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic (Vankov 1978)\". In When NOT, \"The distance-runner sentence\" is now \"The distance-athlete sentence ('distance athletes', not runners)\". Slug unchanged (it says \"distance\", not \"runners\"), so no rename. |\n\n## Missing ideas: placement\n\n| # | idea | placement |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Decision-making and problem-solving (PDF 355-356) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The H/M/L rating, six steps, Maier and Roskin are framed for \"managers or committees\"; the page has no coach, athlete or training example. |\n| 2 | Management versus leadership; Oncken's authority types (PDF 350, 353) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The only sport mention is an illustration of the terms (team captains lead on the field, managers off it); nothing applies it to training. |\n| 3 | Blake-Mouton grid, Tannenbaum-Schmidt continuum, Likert (PDF 353-355) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The grid coordinates are given for generic management styles. The nearby \"applied by managers, leaders and coaches steeped in the traditional ways\" refers to the Fig 6.17 traditional model, as a criticism, not to the grid, and gives no training use. |\n| 4 | Needs theories (PDF 352) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The one athlete note (world-class performances in altered states, Murphy & White 1978) describes transcendence; it is not applied to training. The \"applied with circumspection\" warning concerns Maslow's model in general. |\n| 5 | Endurance monitoring limit (PDF 359) | **Folded into** `claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation` (its When NOT already held the endurance caveat from the same paragraph), with a labelled Inference. |\n\nNo new entry was written, so `_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt` is unchanged.\n\n## Reciprocal links (within 6b files only; all targets exist in the book folder)\n\n- distributed-vs-concentrated → [[claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes]]: added.\n- concentrated-blocks → [[claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality]]: added. [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]] was already in Related; it is now also cited in the conflict paragraph for the PDF 375 duration.\n- mesocycle → [[framework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap]]: added.\n- adaptation-reserve-window → [[principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue]]: added.\n- The back-links from those 6c/6d/6a files to the 6b entries are for their own fixers or the coordinator; I did not edit them.\n\n## Disagreements with the review\n\n1. **Block lengths: `contested` kept, but the conflict is narrower than the review states.** The review calls 3-4 weeks, 4-8 weeks and \"up to 2 months\" one quantity in conflict. On the pages, 4-8 weeks (PDF 305, offered \"for instance\") and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381, a ceiling) agree with each other. The real conflict is 3-4 weeks, which PDF 360 presents as the determined optimum, against blocks up to twice that long in 5.3.3. The entry now says so explicitly. It still counts as a conflict on one quantity, so `contested` stays.\n2. **PDF 375 adds a link the review did not mention.** PDF 375 says the LDTE duration \"is approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\". So the 4-12 week LDTE figure and the 4-12 week stage figure are tied by the book itself; they are still different quantities from block length. Quoted in the entry.\n3. **Bondarchuk page range.** The review's correction text gives \"PDF pp. 334-336 / printed pp. 323-325\". The text layer puts the 6.2.2 heading on PDF 334 and Table 6.1 (its reference and caption) on PDF 335; nothing for either is on 336. The entry says pp. 334-335 / printed 323-324.\n4. **Fig 6.22:** no disagreement. My own measurement agrees with the review (see the reading above).\n5. **Optional items not applied.** Expectancy (Tellier provenance note) and situational leadership (\"Inference:\" prefix) are GO rows with optional suggestions, and arousal's Eysenck/1908 notes need a checked citation. None was applied. I did apply two minor GO-row items: the adaptation-reserve entry (the PDF 359 locator the review asked for, and the Bompa wording, verified against the vault file) and the restorative-stage pointer (a dangling \"above\" in a standalone note).\n\nEvery other review claim held up on the page: Fig 6.12 shaded regions (PDF 348), Fig 6.15 hump B (PDF 351), \"further subdivide\" placement (PDF 357), the \"fundamental unit\" pair (PDF 327, 358), the PDF 359 text matching the image, \"taken much further\" about research (PDF 359), Fig 6.23 dashed lines and no drawn blocks (PDF 361), the PDF 371 medium-qualification sentence, the Zhurbinoi placement and the absence of a Chapter 4 pointer (PDF 362), and \"distance athletes\" (PDF 362).\n\n## Checks\n\nGrep proof, run from the book folder (new wording, one line per change):\n\n```\nframework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md:23:which overlap at fitness state\nframework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md:31:Inference: fitness state is therefore the only route\nheuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md:23:a second hump B on the right-hand slope\nheuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md:18:The book gives no source for the personality difference\nframework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming.md:27:extending it to the complex group is this entry's inference\nprinciple--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md:25:The authors' stated basis is \"modern sporting requirements\"\nprinciple--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md:29:the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:22:whose slope shrinks each year\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:28:Graph A flattens year by year\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:28:they do not express the internal changes\nclaim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md:25:research on adaptation (Folbrot, Selye)\nclaim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md:29:Graph A's slope shrinks each year, consistent with the parabola\nprinciple--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md:22:an unchanging load, plateau\nprinciple--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md:30:loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:Panel B's depression lasts until about weeks 7-9 of 18\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:so it is not required there\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:Contested inside the book (concentrated block length)\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:Different quantities, not part of the conflict\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:which makes the month the working unit\nheuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md:27:as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration\nclaim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md:24:6.2.2 opens on PDF p. 334\nclaim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md:20:Inference: Bondarchuk's study as reported\nprinciple--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md:22:the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\nprinciple--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md:20:accelerate the increase in functional strength (Zhurbinoi, 1978)\nclaim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov.md:14:for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic\n```\n\nOld phrases, count of 6b files still holding each (all 0):\n\n```\nshaded box A: 0\nspikes B and C: 0\nown call to \"further subdivide\" applies: 0\nBatch 6a: 0\nbatch 6a: 0\nnearly straight: 0\ntext layer only: 0\nNot for novices or medium-level: 0\nFigure against text: the figure: 0\nDistance Runners Add: 0\npoint to Chapter 4: 0\n5.3.3 entry above: 0\nhas to be taken much further,\" assuming: 0\n```\n\n`grep -i batch` over the 16 6b files: no matches.\n\nMechanical greps over the 16 scoped files (run under `/bin/bash`):\n\n```\n== em dashes not in section headers:\n(end)\n== header em-dash count per file:\n  16 6\n== wrapped wikilinks:\n(end)\n== CR endings:\n0\n```\n\nAll wikilink targets resolve (the four `old-bull-performance-course--old-bull/...` targets are in the vault under `performance-technology-and-leadership/`).\n\nLint, run from the Flint root:\n\n```\n$ ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\n\nNo 6b file appears in the lint output. The one issue is the known `_book.md` false positive (title and table dashes), outside scope and not edited.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CffosnSFARYSg83YRcf6F","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1d13707-66bf-48b3-ae62-faf2fc47ea9c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:53:52.212Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"e1d13707-66bf-48b3-ae62-faf2fc47ea9c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eca50d28-8512-43f5-a4de-783e8ab372de","agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016FmZAvaJsJ9nMYrArfX9sB","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"3a9f916d-e229-437f-a41d-7ab4cd7d9064","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:53:52.333Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md","content":"# Fixes applied: Supertraining 6.4-6.8.2 (Ch6b), 16 entries\n\nFixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03. Review: `staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md` (round 1, GO AFTER FIXES: 11 FIX rows, 7 numbered fix groups, 4 reciprocal-link suggestions, 5 missing ideas).\nSource checked: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`. I extracted the text of PDF idx 305, 327, 347-362, 370, 371, 375 and 381 with PyMuPDF (`staging/_tmp/f6b_text.txt`). I rendered and opened PDF 305, 348, 351, 358, 359, 360, 361, 362, 375 and 381 (`staging/_renders/f6b_p<N>.png`), plus a 400 dpi crop of Fig 6.22 (`staging/_renders/f6b_p358_fig622_400.png`). Page key: PDF idx = printed + 11.\nScope: the 16 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`. I edited the 11 flagged entries plus two GO entries (`principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window`, for the PDF 359 locator, the Bompa wording and a review-suggested reciprocal link; `heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance`, for a dangling \"entry above\" pointer). No new entries, so the scope file is unchanged (16 lines). No renames. I did not edit `_book.md`, any 6a, 6c or 6d file, or the vault.\n\n## Fig 6.22 reading (decided from the image)\n\nGraph A (thick line, \"Fitness state\") on the 400 dpi crop of PDF 358 / p.347: it starts at about y = 660 px (Year 1 left edge), is at about 440 px at the Year 1/2 boundary, about 285 px at the Year 2/3 boundary and about 200 px at the right edge. The rise is about 225 px in Year 1, about 155 px in Year 2 and about 80 px in Year 3. At the Year 1/2 boundary A sits about 70 px above the straight chord from start to end. So A is a decelerating (concave) curve, consistent with the text's \"parabola whose peak is eventually reached with time\" (PDF 359). No peak is drawn within the three years. The review is right and the writer's \"nearly straight\" reading was wrong; both Fig 6.22 fixes were applied.\n\n| file | what changed |\n|---|---|\n| framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md | **Fix 6 + 5.** The \"(shaded box A)\" and \"(shaded box B)\" parentheticals are removed from the Fig 6.12 walk-through. A new sentence describes \"the shaded band A (Training Load, Training Potential of Loading, Athlete's Fitness State) and the shaded region B (Athlete's Fitness State, Training Effect of Loading, Athlete's External Interactions), which overlap at fitness state\" (checked against the PDF 348 image). Why it works now opens: \"The authors set out a one-way chain (load, fitness state, external interactions) and control at two levels (PDF p. 348 / printed p. 337). Inference: fitness state is therefore the only route from load to result, so both links need measuring.\" |\n| heuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md | **Fix 6.** Fig 6.15 now reads: \"one broad inverted-U ...; a narrow spike A at low arousal; a second hump B on the right-hand slope of the broad curve ('second wind'); and a narrow spike C at high arousal\" (checked against the PDF 351 image). Point 2 adds: \"The book gives no source for the personality difference; it is presented as a general claim ('appears'), not as the authors' finding.\" The optional Eysenck and 1908 provenance notes were not added (they need a checked citation). |\n| framework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming.md | **Fix 6.** When NOT now says the authors call for subdivision (\"One should further subdivide the sports in each of these broad groups\") only within the acyclic and cyclic groups, before they introduce the third group (PDF 357 / p.346), and that \"extending it to the complex group is this entry's inference\". Verified in the text layer: the call sits between the cyclic bullet and \"Finally, one should identify a third group\". |\n| principle--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md | **Fix 5 + 4.** Why it works now reads: \"The authors' stated basis is 'modern sporting requirements' and 'common sense' (PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347); they give no study. Inference: the effects they go on to describe ... unfold over weeks, so microcycle-to-microcycle comparison would misread them.\" The batch 6a sentence is deleted. In its place: the book calls the training session \"the fundamental unit\" in 6.2 (PDF 327 / p.316, confirmed in the text layer) and the mesocycle the fundamental unit in 6.8.1 (PDF 358); \"the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit. Inference: the book does not reconcile the wording\". Link to [[framework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap]] added there and in Related (review's reciprocal-link suggestion). |\n| claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md | **Fix 1 + 7, missing idea 5.** \"a thick, nearly straight rising line A\" is now \"a thick rising line A ... whose slope shrinks each year (steepest in Year 1, flattest in Year 3)\". \"a high-resolution crop\" is now \"a 400 dpi crop\". The \"Figure against text\" sentence is replaced with \"Graph A flattens year by year, in line with the text's 'parabola whose peak is eventually reached with time' (PDF p. 359 / printed p. 348); no peak is drawn within the three years.\" All three \"text layer only\" locators for PDF 359 now read \"checked against the page image\" (I opened the page). Missing idea 5 is folded into the endurance caveat: the problem lies \"in the ability to observe it in the factors used for analysis\", with the full \"measures of aerobic and anaerobic output ... do not express the internal changes associated with adaptation to intense cyclic or acyclic work\" quote, plus a labelled Inference on what that means for conditioning tests. |\n| claim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md | **Fix 1 + 6 + 7.** The PDF 359 locator now reads \"checked against the page image\". Why it works now says research on adaptation (Folbrot, Selye) \"has to be taken much further in its application to the development of sporting mastery, especially in endurance sports\"; until then they assume \"the same, above-mentioned chief mechanisms ...\". When NOT: the \"Page 359 was read from the text layer only\" sentence and the \"graph A looks nearly straight\" clause are deleted, replaced with \"Graph A's slope shrinks each year, consistent with the parabola, but no peak is drawn within the three years (PDF p. 358 / printed p. 347).\" |\n| principle--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md | **GO row, minor items applied.** PDF 359 locator now \"checked against the page image\". The Bompa comparison now reads \"sets out three outcomes of loading (an increasing, varied load, adaptation; an unchanging load, plateau; an excessive one, maladaptation)\", checked against the vault `periodization--bompa/principle--progressive-overload-threshold` (\"a *standard* (unchanging) load ⇒ plateau\"). Related adds the review's reciprocal link [[principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue]]. |\n| framework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md | **Fix 2.** (1) The dip-versus-block sentence is replaced: Panel B's depression lasts until about weeks 7-9 of 18, which fits \"concentrated in the first half of the training phase\" (PDF 360); the figure marks 6-week intervals (dashed lines at weeks 6 and 12) and shows no 3-4 week blocks or 7-10 day pauses, so it does not illustrate the block durations; its x-axis ends at 18 weeks against the text's 18-22 (all checked on the PDF 360 and 361 images). (2) \"Issurin (2016) judged the evidence for Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model insufficient ...\" (the vault Issurin brief, line 51, says the CU model is Verkhoshansky's). (3) \"Not for novices or medium-level athletes, by the authors' own scope\" is replaced with: devised for highly qualified athletes (PDF 360); in 6.9.5 \"both methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification\" (PDF p. 371 / printed p. 360, text layer), \"so it is not required there\". I also changed the When to apply Inference, which said \"distributed loading for medium-level athletes\", to \"distributed loading when performance must hold; at medium qualification the authors say both forms work\". Reciprocal link [[claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes]] added in When NOT and Related. `contested` stays, for the Issurin reason. |\n| heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md | **Fix 3.** The When NOT conflict paragraph is rewritten by quantity. **Concentrated block length (the conflict):** 3-4 weeks (PDF 360, given as the \"determined\" optimum), \"for instance, ... 4-8 week concentrated blocks\" (PDF 305, image checked) and \"a limited period (of up to 2 months)\" (PDF 381, image checked). **Different quantities:** 4-12 week unidirectional *stage* (PDF 305, 381); 4-12 week LDTE duration, \"approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\" (PDF 375 / p.364, image checked); 1-3 week latency (PDF 305); 18-22 week stage to exhaust the CAR (PDF 360); per-quality upper limits in [[claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality]]. The 9-12 week reconciliation is kept as Inference, now framed as linking block length to stage length. New Inference: both 5.3.3 and 6.12.2 define concentration by one month's volume (23-25%, PDF 305 and 381, quoted), so the month is the working unit and \"up to 2 months\" reads as a ceiling. The PDF 381 \"text layer only\" locator is gone. The \"Unclear arithmetic\" note is unchanged. Related adds the time-limits link. `contested` kept (see Disagreements 1). |\n| heuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md | **GO row, minor item applied.** \"as quoted in the 5.3.3 entry above\" is now \"as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]]\". |\n| claim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md | **Fix 4 + 5.** The batch 6a sentence is replaced with \"The 6.2.2 intensity-zone material and Table 6.1 it points to are at PDF pp. 334-335 / printed pp. 323-324 (6.2.2 opens on PDF p. 334; Table 6.1 is on PDF p. 335)\" (checked in the text layer; see Disagreements 3). Why it works now opens \"Inference: Bondarchuk's study as reported does not test intensity at all ...\". |\n| principle--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md | **Fix 5 + 6.** The Zhurbinoi passage is now quoted in full, both sentences, with \"(Zhurbinoi, 1978)\" where the source puts it (closing the second sentence; PDF 362 image). Why it works now reads: \"For the cyclic side the authors cite Zhurbinoi (1978) on strength-endurance (PDF p. 362 / printed p. 351); the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only. Inference: Chapter 4's argument ... supports the same point.\" |\n| claim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov.md | **Fix 6.** Title is now \"Training Emphasis Shifts With Qualification: Sprinters Move From Aerobic Endurance and Speed to Speed Endurance; for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic (Vankov 1978)\". In When NOT, \"The distance-runner sentence\" is now \"The distance-athlete sentence ('distance athletes', not runners)\". Slug unchanged (it says \"distance\", not \"runners\"), so no rename. |\n\n## Missing ideas: placement\n\n| # | idea | placement |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Decision-making and problem-solving (PDF 355-356) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The H/M/L rating, six steps, Maier and Roskin are framed for \"managers or committees\"; the page has no coach, athlete or training example. |\n| 2 | Management versus leadership; Oncken's authority types (PDF 350, 353) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The only sport mention is an illustration of the terms (team captains lead on the field, managers off it); nothing applies it to training. |\n| 3 | Blake-Mouton grid, Tannenbaum-Schmidt continuum, Likert (PDF 353-355) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The grid coordinates are given for generic management styles. The nearby \"applied by managers, leaders and coaches steeped in the traditional ways\" refers to the Fig 6.17 traditional model, as a criticism, not to the grid, and gives no training use. |\n| 4 | Needs theories (PDF 352) | **Not added: not applied to training.** The one athlete note (world-class performances in altered states, Murphy & White 1978) describes transcendence; it is not applied to training. The \"applied with circumspection\" warning concerns Maslow's model in general. |\n| 5 | Endurance monitoring limit (PDF 359) | **Folded into** `claim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation` (its When NOT already held the endurance caveat from the same paragraph), with a labelled Inference. |\n\nNo new entry was written, so `_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt` is unchanged.\n\n## Reciprocal links (within 6b files only; all targets exist in the book folder)\n\n- distributed-vs-concentrated → [[claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes]]: added.\n- concentrated-blocks → [[claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality]]: added. [[heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next]] was already in Related; it is now also cited in the conflict paragraph for the PDF 375 duration.\n- mesocycle → [[framework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap]]: added.\n- adaptation-reserve-window → [[principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue]]: added.\n- The back-links from those 6c/6d/6a files to the 6b entries are for their own fixers or the coordinator; I did not edit them.\n\n## Disagreements with the review\n\n1. **Block lengths: `contested` kept, but the conflict is narrower than the review states.** The review calls 3-4 weeks, 4-8 weeks and \"up to 2 months\" one quantity in conflict. On the pages, 4-8 weeks (PDF 305, offered \"for instance\") and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381, a ceiling) agree with each other. The real conflict is 3-4 weeks, which PDF 360 presents as the determined optimum, against blocks up to twice that long in 5.3.3. The entry now says so explicitly. It still counts as a conflict on one quantity, so `contested` stays.\n2. **PDF 375 adds a link the review did not mention.** PDF 375 says the LDTE duration \"is approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\". So the 4-12 week LDTE figure and the 4-12 week stage figure are tied by the book itself; they are still different quantities from block length. Quoted in the entry.\n3. **Bondarchuk page range.** The review's correction text gives \"PDF pp. 334-336 / printed pp. 323-325\". The text layer puts the 6.2.2 heading on PDF 334 and Table 6.1 (its reference and caption) on PDF 335; nothing for either is on 336. The entry says pp. 334-335 / printed 323-324.\n4. **Fig 6.22:** no disagreement. My own measurement agrees with the review (see the reading above).\n5. **Optional items not applied.** Expectancy (Tellier provenance note) and situational leadership (\"Inference:\" prefix) are GO rows with optional suggestions, and arousal's Eysenck/1908 notes need a checked citation. None was applied. I did apply two minor GO-row items: the adaptation-reserve entry (the PDF 359 locator the review asked for, and the Bompa wording, verified against the vault file) and the restorative-stage pointer (a dangling \"above\" in a standalone note).\n\nEvery other review claim held up on the page: Fig 6.12 shaded regions (PDF 348), Fig 6.15 hump B (PDF 351), \"further subdivide\" placement (PDF 357), the \"fundamental unit\" pair (PDF 327, 358), the PDF 359 text matching the image, \"taken much further\" about research (PDF 359), Fig 6.23 dashed lines and no drawn blocks (PDF 361), the PDF 371 medium-qualification sentence, the Zhurbinoi placement and the absence of a Chapter 4 pointer (PDF 362), and \"distance athletes\" (PDF 362).\n\n## Checks\n\nGrep proof, run from the book folder (new wording, one line per change):\n\n```\nframework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md:23:which overlap at fitness state\nframework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions.md:31:Inference: fitness state is therefore the only route\nheuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md:23:a second hump B on the right-hand slope\nheuristic--arousal-optimum-is-individual-so-fit-restoration-to-personality-and-task-complexity.md:18:The book gives no source for the personality difference\nframework--three-sport-groups-acyclic-cyclic-complex-for-programming.md:27:extending it to the complex group is this entry's inference\nprinciple--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md:25:The authors' stated basis is \"modern sporting requirements\"\nprinciple--mesocycle-not-microcycle-as-the-unit-and-planned-dips-are-not-errors.md:29:the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:22:whose slope shrinks each year\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:28:Graph A flattens year by year\nclaim--four-observations-on-long-term-speed-strength-adaptation.md:28:they do not express the internal changes\nclaim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md:25:research on adaptation (Folbrot, Selye)\nclaim--compensatory-adaptation-is-temporary-and-precedes-stable-adaptation.md:29:Graph A's slope shrinks each year, consistent with the parabola\nprinciple--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md:22:an unchanging load, plateau\nprinciple--load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window.md:30:loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:Panel B's depression lasts until about weeks 7-9 of 18\nframework--distributed-vs-concentrated-loading-two-forms-of-compensatory-adaptation.md:32:so it is not required there\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:Contested inside the book (concentrated block length)\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:Different quantities, not part of the conflict\nheuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery.md:26:which makes the month the working unit\nheuristic--restorative-stage-length-scales-with-homeostatic-disturbance.md:27:as quoted in [[heuristic--allow-restoration\nclaim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md:24:6.2.2 opens on PDF p. 334\nclaim--bondarchuk-50-percent-more-volume-did-not-prolong-training-effect.md:20:Inference: Bondarchuk's study as reported\nprinciple--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md:22:the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\nprinciple--functional-specialisation-is-a-primary-emphasis-not-an-exclusive-energy-system.md:20:accelerate the increase in functional strength (Zhurbinoi, 1978)\nclaim--sprint-and-distance-training-emphasis-shifts-with-qualification-vankov.md:14:for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic\n```\n\nOld phrases, count of 6b files still holding each (all 0):\n\n```\nshaded box A: 0\nspikes B and C: 0\nown call to \"further subdivide\" applies: 0\nBatch 6a: 0\nbatch 6a: 0\nnearly straight: 0\ntext layer only: 0\nNot for novices or medium-level: 0\nFigure against text: the figure: 0\nDistance Runners Add: 0\npoint to Chapter 4: 0\n5.3.3 entry above: 0\nhas to be taken much further,\" assuming: 0\n```\n\n`grep -i batch` over the 16 6b files: no matches.\n\nMechanical greps over the 16 scoped files (run under `/bin/bash`):\n\n```\n== em dashes not in section headers:\n(end)\n== header em-dash count per file:\n  16 6\n== wrapped wikilinks:\n(end)\n== CR endings:\n0\n```\n\nAll wikilink targets resolve (the four `old-bull-performance-course--old-bull/...` targets are in the vault under `performance-technology-and-leadership/`).\n\nLint, run from the Flint root:\n\n```\n$ ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\n\nNo 6b file appears in the lint output. The one issue is the known `_book.md` false positive (title and table dashes), outside scope and not edited.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e1d13707-66bf-48b3-ae62-faf2fc47ea9c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288",