{"parentUuid":"a184faa7-89da-4488-84f7-861c1b53392b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffp69ZpxWVrX9JJ49Cij","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":197366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":286,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6959,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cffp5wntmkzKdVbHepheU","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"18504846-8dde-46a6-9948-187b144c5e98","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:55:38.388Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"18504846-8dde-46a6-9948-187b144c5e98","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3a7c5b2195561b4b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffp69ZpxWVrX9JJ49Cij","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've applied the round-1 review to the Ch6b entries. All 11 FIX rows went in, and none of the review's claims turned out to be wrong on the page. Where I part from the review is on details. The log is at `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md`.\n\n**Fig 6.22, graph A (my reading from a 400 dpi crop of PDF 358):** the line rises about 225 px in Year 1, 155 px in Year 2 and 80 px in Year 3. At the Year 1/2 boundary it sits about 70 px above a straight line from start to end. So it is a slowing curve that matches the text's parabola, with no peak drawn. The review was right and the writer's \"nearly straight\" was wrong, so both Fig 6.22 fixes were applied.\n\n**Per-fix outcome (all applied, each checked on the page image first):**\n1. **Fig 6.22** (`four-observations`, `compensatory`): the false figure-against-text claims are removed and A is described as flattening each year.\n2. **`distributed-vs-concentrated`:**\n   - The Fig 6.23 sentence now compares like with like: the dip runs to about weeks 7-9 of 18, which fits \"first half of the training phase\", and the figure draws no 3-4 week blocks.\n   - The critique line now says Issurin judged Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model.\n   - \"Not for medium-level\" is replaced with the PDF 371 line that both forms work at medium qualification. I checked the image: it says \"are\", where the text layer has \"arc\".\n   - The entry's own \"distributed for medium-level athletes\" line is softened to match.\n3. **`concentrated-blocks`:** the numbers are now sorted by what they measure:\n   - Block length (the conflict): 3-4 weeks (PDF 360), 4-8 weeks (PDF 305) and \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381).\n   - Single-emphasis stage length: 4-12 weeks (PDF 305, 381).\n   - Delayed-effect duration: 4-12 weeks (PDF 375).\n   - Latency to gains: 1-3 weeks. Adaptation-reserve span: 18-22 weeks.\n   - New labelled Inference: both 5.3.3 and 6.12.2 define \"concentrated\" by one month's volume (23-25%), so the month is the working unit.\n4. **\"Batch 6a\" process notes** are removed from `mesocycle` and `bondarchuk`.\n5. **\"Inference:\" labels** are added in `mesocycle`, `functional-specialisation`, `bondarchuk` and `logical-scheme`.\n6. **Source mismatches fixed:** shaded areas A and B in Fig 6.12, curve B as a hump on the slope in Fig 6.15, the unsourced personality claim, \"further subdivide\" limited to two groups, \"taken much further\" refers to research, the Zhurbinoi quote now covers both sentences, and the Vankov title now says \"distance athletes\".\n7. **PDF 359 locators:** all now read \"checked against the page image\". I opened the page myself.\n- **Two small extras in entries the review passed:** the Bompa wording and a PDF 359 locator in `adaptation-reserve-window`, and a dangling \"entry above\" in `restorative-stage`, now a wikilink.\n\n**Disagreements with the review:**\n- **Block-length conflict is narrower than stated.** The 4-8 weeks and \"up to 2 months\" agree with each other. The real conflict is the 3-4 week figure, which PDF 360 calls the determined optimum, against those longer blocks. I kept `contested` and the entry now says this.\n- **Bondarchuk pages:** the material is on PDF 334-335 (printed 323-324), not 334-336.\n- **PDF 375 adds a link the review didn't mention:** the book says the delayed effect lasts about as long as the strength stage. They are still different quantities from block length.\n\n**Missing ideas:** the four management-theory items were not added because the authors do not apply them to training on the page. The only sport mentions are team captains used to illustrate a term, and a criticism of coaches who use the old management model. The PDF 359 point that endurance measures don't show the internal changes of adaptation is folded into `four-observations`.\n\n**Links:** all four suggested links are added within 6b files, and all targets exist. I did not edit any 6a, 6c or 6d file, `_book.md` or the vault.\n\n**Renames:** none. The Vankov slug says \"distance\", not \"runners\", so only its title changed.\n\n**Grep proof** (excerpt; the full block is in the log):\n```\n...logical-scheme...:23:which overlap at fitness state\n...four-observations...:22:whose slope shrinks each year\n...four-observations...:28:Graph A flattens year by year\n...distributed-vs-concentrated...:32:Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model\n...concentrated-blocks...:26:Different quantities, not part of the conflict\n...vankov.md:14:for Distance Athletes the Top-Level Emphasis Is Printed as Anaerobic\n```\nOld phrases (\"shaded box A\", \"nearly straight\", \"text layer only\", \"Batch 6a\", \"Distance Runners Add\" and others): 0 files each. `grep -i batch` over the 16 Ch6b files finds nothing. There are no em dashes outside section headers (each file has exactly 6, all in headers), no wrapped wikilinks, and every link target resolves.\n\n**Lint:**\n```\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\nNo Ch6b file appears in the lint output. The one issue is the known false positive in `_book.md`, which I didn't touch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":197366,"output_tokens":1998,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":50},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":286},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1998,"cache_read_input_tokens":197366,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":286,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffp5wntmkzKdVbHepheU","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"399fc07c-79f7-4695-a1a3-3ab68b11afd7","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:55:47.980Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
